WEBVTT

00:02.335 --> 00:04.665
Shinjitai
I want to believe

00:04.765 --> 00:07.825
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light that I found that day

00:08.305 --> 00:11.045
kimi to kawashita
Because I still have

00:11.045 --> 00:15.705
tatta hitotsuno yakusoku ga arukara
That one promise that I made to you

00:16.115 --> 00:23.105
mou tachidomarazuni aruite yukitai
I want to keep walking, never stopping

00:24.825 --> 00:27.695
Dragon Drive

00:27.695 --> 00:33.215
uresugita kajitsu wo kajiru youni
Like biting into an overripe fruit

00:33.325 --> 00:36.295
yowai jibun ni
I was spoiling myself

00:36.295 --> 00:39.565
amaetsuzukete ita
I was giving in to my weakness

00:40.035 --> 00:44.405
kimi ni deawanakereba
If I hadn't met you

00:44.405 --> 00:46.375
ima mo
I'd still...

00:46.375 --> 00:52.715
kabe wo kowasu koto nado dekinakatta yo
...be unable to break the walls around me

00:54.415 --> 00:56.785
wasurenai
I'll never forget

00:56.785 --> 01:00.015
ano hi kanjita itami
The pain that I felt that day

01:00.325 --> 01:05.325
nido to ano basho modoritakunai
I never want to go back to that place

01:05.325 --> 01:06.915
motto tsuyoku
This strong feeling

01:07.025 --> 01:09.435
shinjitai
I want to believe

01:09.435 --> 01:12.595
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light I found that day

01:12.965 --> 01:18.045
kakkowarui to warawaretemo ii
Let them laugh and call me a loser

01:18.045 --> 01:20.775
bukiyou dakara
Because I'm clumsy

01:20.775 --> 01:28.375
onaji ikikata shika erabenainda
I can only choose to live life this way

01:41.235 --> 01:42.795
My own dragon?

01:42.795 --> 01:44.365
I believe...

01:44.365 --> 01:47.805
...there's a sleeping dragon deep inside
you just waiting to be awakened, Reiji!

01:48.405 --> 01:49.275
W-Wake up...

01:49.275 --> 01:51.005
...dragon sleeping within me!

01:51.005 --> 01:51.975
Wake up!

01:56.215 --> 01:57.945
I wonder what this is?

01:57.945 --> 02:00.545
A really strange one has appeared!

02:00.685 --> 02:02.955
Fly! Fly!

02:02.955 --> 02:04.015
Please fly!

02:04.015 --> 02:06.515
Say your prayers! Go, Kanper!

02:06.755 --> 02:07.485
Wh-What?!

02:07.485 --> 02:09.215
Do it, Chibi!

02:15.665 --> 02:17.825
I thought I'd die.

02:19.605 --> 02:23.125
Promised Dive

02:23.675 --> 02:27.605
- Here, pass it over here!
- Would you hurry up?!

02:27.605 --> 02:30.815
- No, this way!
- Over here!

02:30.815 --> 02:33.615
No matter how I look at it,
that game yesterday...

02:33.615 --> 02:36.415
...was definitely not a dream.

02:36.685 --> 02:38.115
I really...

02:39.385 --> 02:40.955
...won!

02:40.955 --> 02:43.055
Riding that dragon!

02:43.055 --> 02:44.725
Reiji, it's headed your way!

02:44.725 --> 02:45.725
I...

02:45.725 --> 02:48.495
I think I might... really be super cool!

02:48.495 --> 02:49.795
Watch out, Reiji!

02:51.105 --> 02:52.105
Owww...

02:52.105 --> 02:54.535
- Reiji!
- Are you all right?! Hey!

02:54.535 --> 02:56.475
He's passed out with a smile on his face!

02:56.475 --> 02:59.305
- That's creepy!
- Take him to the nurse's office!

02:59.305 --> 03:01.335
Why can't he get it right?

03:04.515 --> 03:08.115
I've made reservations for the two of us
to take part in today's game, Reiji.

03:08.115 --> 03:10.055
From now on, register on your own!

03:10.555 --> 03:11.585
Yeah, yeah!

03:11.585 --> 03:13.215
I really must be a genius.

03:14.525 --> 03:15.855
Are you listening?!

03:19.265 --> 03:22.595
Maiko, I was really something
yesterday, wasn't I?

03:22.595 --> 03:24.325
I must be a genius!

03:24.905 --> 03:27.465
You've repeated that thirty times
since this morning.

03:27.835 --> 03:30.335
I hate to burst your bubble,
but that was beginner's luck!

03:30.335 --> 03:31.275
It was a coincidence!

03:31.275 --> 03:32.405
Just a fluke!

03:32.405 --> 03:33.605
But I won.

03:33.975 --> 03:36.645
So you could say I'm a man of miracles
who has coincidence on his side...

03:36.645 --> 03:38.975
...making the impossible possible.

03:39.515 --> 03:43.785
Could it be that I'm the emperor
of the Dragon Drive, chosen by God?!

03:45.455 --> 03:48.595
I dislike Reiji when he lacks the will
to do anything and just gives up...

03:48.595 --> 03:52.325
...but an elated Reiji, limitless
in his overconfidence, is just as bad.

03:52.325 --> 03:53.625
I said to get over here!

03:53.625 --> 03:56.535
- Who are you kidding?!
- Enough already!

03:56.535 --> 03:59.035
That's the guy who lost to Reiji
in yesterday's match.

03:59.035 --> 04:00.005
You punk!

04:00.005 --> 04:01.735
That's Daisuke Hagiwara of Class A!

04:01.735 --> 04:03.435
And that's Kyoji Tachibana with him!

04:04.035 --> 04:06.945
I hear you're pretty famous around here.

04:07.305 --> 04:10.805
A junior high school student acting like some
big-headed hotshot could get himself hurt.

04:11.715 --> 04:12.505
Bastard!

04:12.845 --> 04:14.445
What's so funny?!

04:14.445 --> 04:19.385
You see, no matter how you compare us,
you've got the bigger head.

04:19.585 --> 04:22.025
Slow down on the jokes,
your face is funny enough.

04:22.025 --> 04:22.885
Why you!

04:26.725 --> 04:29.215
M-My beloved, my sweet honey!

04:29.635 --> 04:31.495
My lovely Maiko Yukino.

04:33.035 --> 04:34.265
D-Darn.

04:34.265 --> 04:38.445
It's that guy again,
standing next to my Maiko!

04:38.445 --> 04:43.275
I've gotta make an impression on Maiko
by showing her how cool I am!

04:43.275 --> 04:43.865
Okay!

04:44.345 --> 04:45.275
Hey, hey, hey!

04:45.645 --> 04:47.845
Don't think you can do whatever you like!

04:47.845 --> 04:51.145
Aren't you embarrassed acting like that
in broad daylight?!

04:52.955 --> 04:54.885
- Bastard!
- Get him!

05:03.295 --> 05:04.335
You!

05:04.335 --> 05:05.965
You asked for it!

05:10.075 --> 05:11.195
Oww!

05:17.215 --> 05:20.345
D-Damn. You're gonna pay for this.

05:20.685 --> 05:23.415
Oh, boy. Look at you.

05:23.415 --> 05:25.215
Hey, are you okay? Can you stand up?

05:26.185 --> 05:29.095
That's the voice of my sweet angel!

05:29.095 --> 05:32.585
She's actually nursing me.
I am such a fortunate guy!

05:33.965 --> 05:37.035
What did you think you were doing?
Straighten up, will ya?

05:37.035 --> 05:39.795
As they say, yesterday's foe is today's friend.

05:40.765 --> 05:42.205
Don't! Don't get any closer!

05:42.435 --> 05:44.425
Don't touch me with those filthy hands!

05:44.845 --> 05:46.245
That was awesome.

05:46.245 --> 05:48.535
You're Kyoji of Class A, aren't you?!

05:48.815 --> 05:51.435
So, you've heard of me?

05:51.685 --> 05:53.115
Of course I have.

05:53.115 --> 05:57.105
A super sports star, strong fighter,
and popular among the girls.

05:57.215 --> 05:59.445
There's no way anyone could not know you.

06:01.355 --> 06:03.345
You're the celebrity.

06:03.655 --> 06:05.995
I saw you, in yesterday's Dragon Drive.

06:06.195 --> 06:07.195
What?

06:07.195 --> 06:10.665
You were watching my genius skills?

06:10.665 --> 06:12.305
Boy, am I embarrassed...

06:12.305 --> 06:14.765
Why didn't you say so sooner?!

06:14.905 --> 06:17.375
Then I take it you play Dragon Drive, too?

06:17.875 --> 06:20.465
Well, a modest interest, I'd say.

06:20.945 --> 06:23.875
I'd be honored to have you
teach me in a game sometime.

06:24.615 --> 06:26.145
Okay! Okay!

06:26.145 --> 06:29.115
Let me know if there's anything
you don't understand!

06:29.455 --> 06:31.415
See ya! Bye!

06:32.955 --> 06:33.685
Hey.

06:33.685 --> 06:35.895
Why so respectful to a nothing like him?

06:35.895 --> 06:38.585
You'd have no problem beating him
with a single blow.

06:41.695 --> 06:44.635
Kyoji seems like a nice guy.

06:44.905 --> 06:46.905
I thought he'd be more frightening to talk to.

06:46.905 --> 06:48.135
Really?

06:48.575 --> 06:50.605
Just what are you implying?

06:50.605 --> 06:51.795
Nothing.

06:52.075 --> 06:54.375
Because he's so perfect that...

06:54.375 --> 06:57.645
...he comes across as kinda
spooky, kinda hard to trust.

06:57.645 --> 07:00.215
"Perfect"?
You're sure direct with your words.

07:00.215 --> 07:01.215
Oh, boy.

07:01.215 --> 07:04.585
The way you pile on the compliments,
even I'm starting to get embarrassed.

07:04.585 --> 07:07.185
I'm not talking about you!

07:07.185 --> 07:08.555
I-Is that so?

07:09.695 --> 07:12.055
I read your report.

07:12.425 --> 07:13.985
Reiji Ozora.

07:14.625 --> 07:18.805
If what you say is true, about him being
in sync with his dragon in his first game...

07:18.805 --> 07:20.065
...then yes, that's significant.

07:20.065 --> 07:20.965
Isn't it?

07:20.965 --> 07:24.495
The only person who's done that
to this point is Hikaru Himuro.

07:24.845 --> 07:26.005
Maybe that boy also...

07:26.305 --> 07:29.745
But don't you think it
might've been a coincidence?

07:29.745 --> 07:33.215
By some chance, Reiji Ozora's movements
just happened to match those of the dragon.

07:33.215 --> 07:34.215
No way!

07:34.215 --> 07:36.205
I saw it with my own eyes!

07:36.855 --> 07:39.655
Well, since you seem to feel
pretty strongly about it...

07:39.925 --> 07:41.855
...I'll observe him closely.

07:41.855 --> 07:46.155
We'll find out if he's an unpolished
diamond or nothing but a lucky boy.

07:46.465 --> 07:49.055
You'll realize soon enough!

07:49.935 --> 07:51.155
It's him. He's here.

07:54.875 --> 07:55.975
Wow.

07:55.975 --> 07:58.435
All kinds of functions for the game.

07:58.945 --> 08:00.475
Ranking:
1 (1) Hikaru Himuro/2(2) Sayaka Towa
Hm?! A ranking chart?

08:00.475 --> 08:02.675
Ranking:
3(5) Kyoji Tachibana/4(-) Ichiro Sumishiba
First place is Hikaru Himuro.

08:02.675 --> 08:03.745
Weird name.

08:03.745 --> 08:05.975
Wh-What a rude thing to say!

08:06.185 --> 08:08.655
He's got game and he's got the looks.
Enough to give you the shivers!

08:08.655 --> 08:10.985
He's one incredible, cool player!

08:10.985 --> 08:13.325
I thought you disliked
those who are perfect.

08:13.325 --> 08:15.525
Mr. Himuro's different!

08:15.525 --> 08:20.095
He stands above the champions
of Blocks A, B and C.

08:20.095 --> 08:23.695
He's the accumulative champion,
the reigning Super Champion!

08:23.835 --> 08:25.595
Huh? What's this?

08:26.035 --> 08:27.595
A-Block Ranking
1 (1) Kyoji Tachibana/2(2) Ichiro Sumishiba
3(-) Hihime Umatani/4(-)Ginji Dekiyama

08:28.275 --> 08:30.765
This Kyoji Tachibana,
is he the Kyoji we know?!

08:30.975 --> 08:33.035
He's champion of Block A!

08:33.205 --> 08:35.475
You're right. When'd he become champion?

08:35.875 --> 08:40.975
But even that Kyoji Tachibana
is no match for Mr. Himuro.

08:41.015 --> 08:42.885
Whoa, far out!

08:43.085 --> 08:44.585
What is it this time?

08:44.585 --> 08:47.285
Look! It's even equipped with a navigator!

08:47.655 --> 08:49.225
Oh, that.

08:49.225 --> 08:53.385
If you use it during the game,
you can tell where the other players are.

08:54.125 --> 08:57.655
Then I can come to your rescue
whenever you're in trouble!

09:03.335 --> 09:05.005
My stomach!

09:05.005 --> 09:09.245
You're killing me!

09:09.245 --> 09:10.675
What's so funny?

09:11.075 --> 09:13.785
We know very well that's not possible.

09:13.785 --> 09:16.915
My Gholaoh is many levels
above your dragon.

09:17.185 --> 09:18.525
I told you!

09:18.525 --> 09:20.525
Things are different from now on.

09:20.525 --> 09:22.855
I'm now the chosen hero!

09:22.855 --> 09:23.925
Not again.

09:23.925 --> 09:27.165
Let me ask you, have you ever
come to my rescue before?

09:27.165 --> 09:28.125
Don't worry.

09:28.125 --> 09:30.155
I'm not counting on you to be my rescuer.

09:31.235 --> 09:32.235
Hey!

09:32.235 --> 09:37.065
I'm offering you help here, so why can't
you accept it and show some gratitude?!

09:43.175 --> 09:45.145
I'll tell you this much...

09:45.145 --> 09:48.635
You have a bad habit of making
promises that you can't even keep!

09:50.055 --> 09:52.045
Why's she mad at me all of a sudden?

09:52.425 --> 09:54.015
That wasn't nice of her!

09:56.725 --> 09:58.365
That was beginner's luck!

09:58.365 --> 10:00.125
It was a coincidence, just a fluke!

10:00.525 --> 10:01.515
Wow!

10:01.865 --> 10:03.395
What's with this card?

10:03.395 --> 10:04.935
I've never seen one like it before.

10:04.935 --> 10:07.835
And the dragon looks really weak.

10:07.835 --> 10:08.925
Is it of any use?

10:09.305 --> 10:10.475
Who are you?!

10:10.475 --> 10:12.575
Attacking me with a choke sleeper hold?!

10:12.575 --> 10:13.765
Cut it out!

10:14.345 --> 10:17.075
Don't you know Ichiro Sumishiba?

10:17.275 --> 10:18.805
Well, not that I mind.

10:19.545 --> 10:21.945
Ichiro... Sumishiba?

10:22.285 --> 10:23.775
A-Block Ranking
1 (1) Kyoji Tachibana/2(2) Ichiro Sumishiba
3(-) Hihime Umatani/4(-) Ginji Dekiyama

10:24.255 --> 10:26.685
He's that Ichiro guy
who's ranked number two!

10:26.885 --> 10:28.825
Look at this card, everybody!

10:30.295 --> 10:33.165
It looks really weak,
but it could be kind of rare.

10:33.165 --> 10:35.995
Hey, give it back!
Give that back to me!

10:36.295 --> 10:38.065
You're making me angry!

10:38.535 --> 10:41.125
- Give it back!
- Why so excited? Just hand it over for a sec!

10:44.705 --> 10:45.695
Kyoji.

10:45.975 --> 10:47.035
Kyoji!

10:47.345 --> 10:51.405
You're not a little child,
so stop acting like one.

10:53.815 --> 10:56.585
Go ahead and act like a big shot
while you still have a chance.

10:56.585 --> 11:01.025
Today's the day I'll defeat you
to become champion.

11:05.225 --> 11:06.955
Thank you, Kyoji.

11:07.465 --> 11:09.235
But what a surprise.

11:09.235 --> 11:12.405
I would've never guessed
you were the Block A champion.

11:12.405 --> 11:14.235
You really can do everything.

11:14.235 --> 11:15.335
I'm impressed!

11:15.335 --> 11:17.375
Impressed? Why?

11:17.375 --> 11:19.435
You're champion. Yeah, champion.

11:21.175 --> 11:24.375
Well, I don't see it
as that much of a big deal.

11:25.245 --> 11:27.385
Well, maybe, but...

11:27.385 --> 11:29.315
It's the moment you've been waiting for!

11:29.455 --> 11:33.085
We will now begin today's
second Dragon Drive match!

11:33.085 --> 11:34.855
- This is a battle game where players pilot...
- Anyway, try to go easy on me.

11:34.855 --> 11:38.085
...their respective dragons in a virtual world!
- Anyway, try to go easy on me.

11:38.225 --> 11:41.865
Because it's played in a battle royale format,
players may battle whomever they like.

11:41.865 --> 11:44.165
They can also play by avoiding opponents!

11:44.165 --> 11:47.605
But if all you do is run away, you won't
accumulate any experience points!

11:47.605 --> 11:52.305
Any player defeating all opponents within
regulation time will be granted bonus points.

11:52.305 --> 11:53.895
Good luck to you all!

11:54.375 --> 11:57.405
Now, everyone,
take your designated positions!

12:04.215 --> 12:05.885
Control tower!

12:05.885 --> 12:09.015
Keep a record on Reiji's performance.

12:09.725 --> 12:11.855
Sure, although I doubt he'll get far.

12:12.195 --> 12:16.225
The probability of Reiji Ozora, a beginner,
surviving in a game against these players...

12:17.235 --> 12:18.525
Z ero percent.

12:19.365 --> 12:21.235
Is everybody ready?

12:21.235 --> 12:23.105
Insert your cards into your cell phones.

12:24.505 --> 12:26.595
Now, please secure your helmets!

12:27.875 --> 12:28.675
Ten minutes.

12:30.845 --> 12:34.445
I think I'll defeat everyone here
within ten minutes.

12:51.095 --> 12:53.105
Okay then, let's get started!

12:53.105 --> 12:54.565
Let's begin the game!

12:55.835 --> 12:57.705
D-Break!

13:14.225 --> 13:16.345
D-Mode complete.

13:17.955 --> 13:18.945
Where am I?

13:22.365 --> 13:24.065
I'm not where I was the last time.

13:24.065 --> 13:28.125
So the starting point is different every time.

13:31.605 --> 13:36.105
How in the world could you possibly
get yourself stuck in a place like that?

13:39.485 --> 13:41.675
Try not to be such a nuisance, would you?!

13:51.055 --> 13:51.995
What speed!

13:58.605 --> 14:00.265
Please, stop!

14:00.265 --> 14:01.535
I'm begging you!

14:03.135 --> 14:04.905
I give up!

14:05.245 --> 14:07.405
Stop, or you'll end up killing my dragon!

14:21.085 --> 14:23.285
Misawa, game over.

14:25.625 --> 14:26.885
One down!

14:27.365 --> 14:28.795
That's terrible.

14:29.035 --> 14:30.395
Really terrible.

14:30.395 --> 14:32.455
That girl had already given up!

14:32.665 --> 14:34.895
Why did you have to finish that dragon off?

14:36.735 --> 14:38.775
Don't you understand the rules?

14:38.775 --> 14:41.865
Unless you defeat the enemy,
you don't get any experience points.

14:42.575 --> 14:45.915
That may be true, but what pleasure
is there winning that way?!

14:45.915 --> 14:47.745
This is supposed to be a game!

14:49.215 --> 14:51.115
That's none of your concern.

14:51.555 --> 14:53.575
I'm free to play the game however I want to.

14:54.255 --> 14:58.385
You'd better worry about yourself
before worrying about others.

14:58.595 --> 15:00.785
Judging from your reaction,
you'll never survive the game.

15:02.835 --> 15:06.795
I would never dream of surviving
this game playing it the way you do!

15:07.105 --> 15:08.675
You fool.

15:08.675 --> 15:10.875
It shows that you're only a beginner.

15:10.875 --> 15:14.105
Well, I'll give you a break
and leave you to the very end.

15:14.105 --> 15:15.805
So good luck until then.

15:19.185 --> 15:21.415
Damn, he makes me so mad!

15:21.415 --> 15:22.975
We'll go after him, Chibi!

15:24.985 --> 15:27.115
Yet he's still struggling over there.

15:32.665 --> 15:33.825
You're too heavy!

15:34.795 --> 15:36.465
Anyway, we're going after him!

15:36.465 --> 15:37.865
Let's go!

15:43.035 --> 15:44.205
Darn it!

15:44.205 --> 15:46.605
Where'd that jerk go?

15:46.605 --> 15:47.835
I know!

15:48.815 --> 15:50.905
This is where the navigator comes in handy.

15:54.485 --> 15:56.685
Why are they being deleted,
one after another?

15:56.685 --> 15:58.055
Name | Dragon | Status
Takashi Shimono | Kiikaisa | ALIVE
Haruko Misawa | Goshorakuurin | ALIVE

15:58.055 --> 16:00.175
Name | Dragon | Status
Haruko Misawa | Goshorakuurin | DEAD
Ichiro Sumishia | Junrah-anshi | ALIVE

16:00.455 --> 16:03.785
I think I'll defeat everyone here
within ten minutes.

16:04.825 --> 16:06.555
That guy was serious.

16:06.995 --> 16:07.995
Damn!

16:07.995 --> 16:09.935
I'd better hurry, or else!

16:11.735 --> 16:12.605
Chibi!

16:12.605 --> 16:14.105
You've got wings!

16:14.105 --> 16:15.895
Use 'em as you did yesterday, so we can fly!

16:17.775 --> 16:19.565
I-I'm telling you! Fly!

16:22.975 --> 16:24.015
Let me explain.

16:24.015 --> 16:26.315
With your wings!
You... You know! Vroom!

16:26.315 --> 16:27.805
You fly, like a bird.

16:28.215 --> 16:29.085
Get it?!

16:33.955 --> 16:35.145
You do understand.

16:36.025 --> 16:36.725
All right!

16:36.725 --> 16:39.285
There's nothing as satisfying
as speeding through the skies!

16:40.065 --> 16:41.065
Or so I thought.

16:41.065 --> 16:45.155
But this isn't speedy at all!

16:53.605 --> 16:56.305
Gholaoh's pain from his
leg injury is increasing!

16:56.375 --> 16:58.975
I didn't expect that earlier hit
to slow him down so much.

17:01.115 --> 17:05.075
They believe they can get
away from me with that injury!

17:08.325 --> 17:09.485
Maiko!

17:10.125 --> 17:12.195
Reiji Ozora?
Maiko Yukino Gholaoh

17:12.195 --> 17:15.095
At this rate, Maiko's gonna be defeated.

17:15.935 --> 17:18.195
But I can't catch up to them with Chibi.

17:18.805 --> 17:22.235
Then I can come to your rescue
whenever you're in trouble!

17:22.235 --> 17:26.225
You have a bad habit of making
promises that you can't even keep!

17:27.545 --> 17:28.775
Darn it!

17:28.775 --> 17:30.435
What should I do?!

17:35.045 --> 17:36.035
This is it!

17:50.035 --> 17:52.205
Let's put an end to this game of tag!

17:52.205 --> 17:54.765
I'll finish you off in one move!

18:02.515 --> 18:04.065
This is frightening!

18:06.445 --> 18:08.245
H-Hey, Chibi, don't shake it!

18:08.245 --> 18:09.715
I could fall!

18:16.495 --> 18:20.055
You know, you shouldn't scare me like that!

18:22.495 --> 18:23.935
Listen, Chibi!

18:24.095 --> 18:26.565
Use your wings as we both jump off to fly.

18:26.935 --> 18:27.905
Got that?!

18:29.275 --> 18:31.535
"Squeak"?! Come on,
don't give me that!

18:31.535 --> 18:34.565
I'm scared as heck, so I'm
counting on you to do this right!

18:35.005 --> 18:36.775
Leave it to me, Maiko.

18:36.775 --> 18:38.375
I'll get it for you!

18:48.525 --> 18:49.925
That's right.

18:49.925 --> 18:52.515
That time as well... I couldn't
jump into the river in front of me.

18:55.935 --> 18:57.195
This'll finish you!

18:57.635 --> 19:01.095
You have a bad habit of making
promises that you can't even keep!

19:03.305 --> 19:05.035
You liar!

19:06.775 --> 19:09.335
Let's go, Chibi!

19:11.115 --> 19:12.545
What the!

19:12.745 --> 19:14.875
Go!

19:20.985 --> 19:23.325
Hey, L! Terminate Reiji Ozora's controls!

19:23.325 --> 19:26.555
It may be a virtual world, but a fall
from that height will cause mental damage!

19:27.565 --> 19:30.755
- Not yet.
- Not yet! I still haven't!

19:31.395 --> 19:34.835
I still haven't fulfilled
my promise to Maiko!

19:35.235 --> 19:36.435
Chibi.

19:36.435 --> 19:38.405
Lend me your strength!

19:51.685 --> 19:53.625
He's attacking?

19:54.325 --> 19:56.315
Guard Scale!

19:57.955 --> 20:01.415
Don't think that a measly attack like that
will get through Junrah-anshi's defense!

20:06.465 --> 20:07.595
Mr. Himuro!

20:08.065 --> 20:09.365
It's Hikaru Himuro!

20:16.415 --> 20:18.645
Junrah-anshi is being overpowered?!

20:28.555 --> 20:30.545
Very well done.

20:32.295 --> 20:33.355
Gotcha!

20:44.735 --> 20:45.945
Th-That's impossible.

20:45.945 --> 20:47.845
His power's increasing!

20:48.205 --> 20:49.675
H-How could this be?!

20:49.675 --> 20:52.115
Guard Scale can't outlast this!

20:54.185 --> 20:55.445
Ichiro!

20:55.445 --> 20:58.855
You've already gone way over
the ten minutes you promised!

21:00.225 --> 21:01.155
Why?

21:01.155 --> 21:04.125
How could something so little
have so much power?!

21:05.625 --> 21:08.655
I-It's impossible!

21:15.935 --> 21:18.065
A-Amazing...

21:18.335 --> 21:19.675
Maiko!

21:20.075 --> 21:22.705
With that, I'm no longer a liar!

21:23.075 --> 21:26.705
This time, I finally fulfilled
my promise to you!

21:29.055 --> 21:30.915
Oh, oh, oh, oh!

21:31.885 --> 21:33.355
Are you all right?

21:33.825 --> 21:34.985
Well, S?

21:34.985 --> 21:36.195
You saw it, didn't you?

21:36.195 --> 21:37.785
That's the power the kid possesses.

21:57.075 --> 21:59.815
Taikutsu datta
I was bored

21:59.815 --> 22:02.585
okubyou datta
I was a coward

22:02.585 --> 22:06.545
dareka wo jibun wo kizutsukete ita
I was hurting someone and myself

22:07.985 --> 22:10.755
tsuyogari itte
I tried to hide my weakness

22:10.755 --> 22:12.955
wagamama itte
I was being selfish

22:13.395 --> 22:17.525
doushiyoumonai kimochi mamoritsuzukete
Protecting the uncontrollable feeling

22:18.935 --> 22:21.605
otona ni natte
I became an adult

22:21.605 --> 22:24.335
kimi to deatte
Then I met you

22:24.335 --> 22:28.335
mune no sumikko yawarakaku natte
My heart got softened

22:29.645 --> 22:32.145
setsunaku natta
Longing for love

22:32.145 --> 22:35.145
dakishime atta
We embraced each other

22:35.145 --> 22:40.055
hakkiri mamorubeki mono wo mitsuketa
I finally knew what I wanted to protect

22:40.685 --> 22:43.425
tatta hitotsu no yuuki ga
Only one courage

22:43.425 --> 22:46.195
tatta hitotsu no kotoba ga
Just one word

22:46.195 --> 22:50.855
futari owaranai yume e to hakobu
Take us to an endless dream

22:51.565 --> 22:54.335
hon no chiisana yasashisa ga
Only a small kindness

22:54.335 --> 22:57.005
hon no wazuka na sasayaki ga
Only a small whisper

22:57.005 --> 23:01.665
futari wo sotto tsutsunde kureru
Wrap us gently

23:02.315 --> 23:06.835
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:07.745 --> 23:13.445
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:15.825 --> 23:18.415
Next Episode

23:18.955 --> 23:21.495
Oh, boy. I won again!

23:21.495 --> 23:22.965
I might really be a genius!

23:24.995 --> 23:25.465
Huh?

23:25.465 --> 23:28.705
Don't be so overconfident if I don't wanna
be defeated by Daisuke Hagiwara, you say?

23:28.705 --> 23:32.365
And that Mr. Perfect,
Kyoji Tachibana, is also glaring at me.

23:32.475 --> 23:34.635
Does this mean the next battle
will be two against one?!

23:35.245 --> 23:37.805
Next on Dragon Drive,
Revenge.

23:38.215 --> 23:39.945
Okay, let's do it, Chibisuke!

23:41.145 --> 23:42.755
What? Go ahead and do it without you?

23:42.755 --> 23:45.485
Revenge
You mustn't say such things!
